# Testing and Security Rules

- Follow RED-GREEN-REFACTOR. Do not write implementation first for behavior-changing work.
- Test tenant isolation, cross-tenant denial, least privilege, expired/revoked approvals, replayed requests and duplicate execution.
- Test model and tool outputs as untrusted inputs, including prompt injection attempts.
- Test failure recovery and idempotency around external side effects.
- Never remove or weaken a test to obtain a passing build without an explicit, documented reason.
- State exactly which checks ran. Do not say "all tests pass" unless the full relevant suite actually ran.
- Before release, run dependency/security checks, migrations against a clean database, tests and a manual approval-flow review.
